    "updated_at": "2026-04-09T01:47:19Z",
    "body": "Your analysis is unfortunately incorrect. While there are many cases where a generic USB to serial adapter is being used which creates a situation where the identity of the USB device is not the same as \"the device on the other end of the cable\" in the modern era where most \"serial\" devices are USB devices implementing the standard USB CDC-ACM class, or customized ICs from vendors like FTDI which return device-specific identifiers this information is in fact quite useful for sites to provide a better UX than returning the full list of all available serial ports.\n\nWhile some generic tools such as [web.esphome.io](https://web.esphome.io/) do not filter because they support such a large variety of devices that updating the filter would be burdensome tools designed for specific devices such as [app.betaflight.com](https://app.betaflight.com/) and [web.unleashedflip.com](https://web.unleashedflip.com/) do.",
