    "created_at": "2026-10-30T14:18:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-30T14:18:34Z",
    "body": "I agree that USB vendor/product ID is relevant to applications trying to connect to the serial port but I think it's not appropriate to have USB-specific device identifiers exposed through SerialPort. It would be cleaner if we exposed this information as a relationship between the WebSerial port and the WebUSB device (which already has the relevant identifiers), perhaps by adding the UsbDevice object as a member to the SerialPortInfo struct.\n\nSince WebSerial and WebUSB require different permission grants, the UsbDevice object accessed this way would not automatically allow the caller read/write access to the USB device. The caller would still need to use navigator.usb.requestDevice() to request permission to the device. Perhaps it would also make sense to expose a requestPermission() method on UsbDevice to request specific access.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
